# Java Coding Standards

## Teaching-Quality Code
This is a learning project. Every file must be understandable by someone learning architecture.

- **No Lombok** — write explicit getters/setters. The user is learning Java patterns.
- **Java 21 Records** for DTOs — immutable, auto-generated methods.
- **Entities** use classes (not records) because JPA needs mutable state.
- **Comment every non-obvious design decision** with SPEC REF or WHY blocks.

## Patterns
- **No unnecessary interfaces** — if there's only one implementation, use a class.
- **Constructor injection** — no `@Autowired` on fields.
- **`@Service`, `@Repository`, `@Component`** — always annotate Spring beans.
- **`@Transactional(readOnly = true)`** on read-only service classes.

## Forbidden
- No `float`/`double` for money (see bigdecimal-precision rule)
- No `System.out.println` — use SLF4J logger
- No wildcard imports (`import java.util.*`)
- No abbreviations in names (`txn` is OK for transactions, but not `amt` for amount)
